The one-page-route requirement applies to public content pages, not every HTTP endpoint in the application.

Working contact forms, quote forms, security features, redirects, sitemaps, robots rules, and other required server functionality may use the appropriate Next.js route handlers or framework conventions.

Do not create separate public `page.tsx` files for each content URL.

Ensure there are no conflicting route files that prevent the optional catch-all route from working.

